CloudBurrow patch 49 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1508).

The bug: a STRING column tables.insert gave a collation ('und:ci') was
made in the engine without it, so its values compared case-sensitively;
and a column CREATE TABLE collated (its COLLATE, or the table's DEFAULT
COLLATE) read back from tables.get with no collation.
The fix: CreateTable writes the column's COLLATE, which the engine
compares its values by (googlesqlite patch 0059), and addTableMetadata
records the engine's collation of a CREATE TABLE's column. Its test
server/collation_test.go fails without it.

